courses=[
('excel','01','Excel for Data Analytics','KEEP · SELECT CHAPTERS','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pCJ15nGFgVg','https://github.com/lukebarousse/Excel_Data_Analytics_Course','Formulas/functions, charts, tables, PivotTables, Power Query, Power Pivot and two projects are present in the published outline.','Prioritise chapters 2–5 and 7. Add UK date parsing, reconciliation, exception logs and a repeatable month-file refresh. Revisit basics only if your diagnostic fails.','Solver, Scenario Manager, Goal Seek and deeper Power Pivot are useful later, not blockers before junior reporting applications.','The creator lists free videos/files but paid supporter problems and certificates. If individual Excel files fail, download the repository ZIP or use the creator’s alternate file link.'),
('sql','02','SQL foundations + selected intermediate','REPLACE SOLE RESOURCE','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7mz73uXD9DA','https://www.lukebarousse.com/sql','The original 2018 freeCodeCamp course lists MySQL basics, joins, nested queries and database design. Its published chapters do not include CTEs or window functions.','Use Luke’s foundations course for analyst queries, CASE and CTEs. Supplement window/date/cleaning topics with '+A('https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QKIGsShyEsQ','selected Intermediate SQL lessons')+' and the official T-SQL window lesson.','Do not spend time on triggers, database administration or a second full beginner course. Keep one primary database and a short dialect bridge.','PostgreSQL is the main course dialect. The free starter job dataset is historical 2023 data, not evidence of today’s London or Brighton market. Supporter exercises/certificates are paid.'),
('pbi','03','Power BI for Data Analytics','KEEP + OPERATIONS PACK','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FwjaHCVNBWA','https://github.com/lukebarousse/PowerBI_Data_Analytics_Course','Published modules include Grand Tour, visualisations, Power Query and DAX, plus star-schema/dashboard projects.','Explicitly add workspace roles/access, gateway and scheduled refresh concepts, a Desktop RLS test, Performance Analyzer, mobile layout and accessibility. Use current Microsoft Learn guidance.','Do not assume the creator’s “PL-300 aligned” description guarantees full current exam coverage. Newer exam topics need a separate exam checklist if you choose certification.','Use the creator’s '+A('https://lukeb.co/powerbi-files','complete course-file link')+'; the repository warns that some large files are missing. Some Service exercises require a suitable account/licence; no paid sharing is required for the portfolio.'),
('python','04','Python for Data Analytics','KEEP · LATER IN SEQUENCE','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wUSDVGivd-8','https://github.com/lukebarousse/Python_Data_Analytics_Course','The outline covers basics, pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, advanced cleaning/manipulation and a project.','Prioritise functions, dates, CSVs, missing values, groupby, merge validation, readable plots and reproducible export. Add one small test fixture and rerun from a clean environment.','Defer deep OOP, machine learning, scraping and advanced plotting unless target roles justify them. Do not postpone Excel/BI applications until every Python chapter is complete.','Use current notebooks when package APIs differ from the video. Free videos/code do not imply every practice problem or certificate is free.'),
('stats','05','Statistics + official guidance','KEEP + APPLIED TASKS','https://www.khanacademy.org/math/statistics-probability','https://www.ons.gov.uk/','Khan Academy is a broad reference, not a role-specific analyst syllabus; use only the topics your checkpoint requires.','Practise denominators, weighted averages, percent vs percentage points, bias, uncertainty, correlation and plain-English communication on your own data.','Do not add a full probability or data-science qualification. Introductory test reasoning is enough unless a role asks for deeper inference.','Complement learning with '+A('https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/uk-gdpr-guidance-and-resources/data-protection-principles/a-guide-to-the-data-protection-principles/','ICO principles')+' and the published methodology for the public dataset you use.')]
