# Detailed standalone audit report.
lines=['# UK Data Analyst Roadmap — Market, Course & Syllabus Audit','**Reviewed: 18 October 2026 · Target: South-East London, Brighton/Hove and the wider South East**','',
'## Executive recommendation','Keep **Excel → SQL → Power BI → defensible projects**, with statistics, data quality and communication throughout. Keep Python/pandas as a useful later addition, but do not make every entry application wait for it. The previous plan had a sound stack but a genuine resource-to-syllabus mismatch: the old SQL link did not support all the CTE/window checkpoints. Power BI operational tasks also needed to be explicit.','',
'No separate agent partners were available. This audit uses three passes by the same assistant: hiring relevance, curriculum alignment, and usability. It is not an independent panel review.','',
'## Scope and limits','Eight purposefully chosen advert profiles were reviewed: five junior/entry-route examples and three experienced-role comparators. This is not a representative sample, vacancy census or a basis for skill-frequency percentages. Full text, employer search-index excerpts and unavailable pages are labelled below. Local SE London examples were experienced roles, so they do not establish a large junior market. Course review used published outlines, files and creator pages—not a minute-by-minute viewing of all videos.','',
'## 1. Regional evidence and what it means']
for i,d in enumerate(ev['adverts']):lines += [f'### {i+1:02}. {d["employer"]} — {d["role"]}',f'- **Geography:** {d["region"]}.',f'- **Level:** {d["level"]}.',f'- **Status:** {d["status"]}.',f'- **Evidence access:** {d["access"]}.',f'- **Signals:** {d["signals"]}.',f'- **Decision for the roadmap:** {d["decision"]}',f'- **Source:** [{1 if d["key"] in ["edf","lg","kreston","7im","oxleas"] else 2 if d["key"]=="lewisham" else 24 if d["key"]=="metlife" else 1}]({d["url"]})','']
